[3.003, "o", "\u001b[H \u001b[C         \u001b[C                                                                                                           \u001b[C      \u001b[C                       \u001b[2;1H \u001b[116C                                 \u001b[3;1H \u001b[116C                                 \u001b[4;1H\u001b[94m1.\u001b[93m stealc-v2-family-intel\u001b[97m (family-intel, new) — Candidate 2. Before saving I spot-verified its distinctive claims against the forum's solved threads:\u001b[39m \u001b[5;1H\u001b[97mthe sRDI MZ-stub/reflective-loader ABE helper and Early-Bird APC injection (!79, !85), WinINet-not-WinHttp with decoy decrypted names (!125, !141),\u001b[39m   \u001b[6;1H\u001b[97mnlohmann JSON builder (!127), CIS locale gate (!102), and ComputerName+UserName named event (!104) — all code-verified. Per the scoped-negative\u001b[39m       \u001b[7;1H\u001b[97mdiscipline, \"no RC4 on wire,\" \"no persistence,\" and \"no anti-VM\" are written as observations about the verified build, not family invariants.\u001b[39m         \u001b[8;1H"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[97mNamed/tagged with the family name as family-intel memories should be.\u001b[48C\u001b[39m                                 \u001b[9;1H\u001b[94m2.\u001b[93m crt-fid-triage-of-detector-api-hits\u001b[97m (workflow, new) — Candidate 3. Generic FID-first triage rule for static-CRT MSVC binaries; includes the caveat\u001b[39m \u001b[10;1H\u001b[97mthat a CRT false positive clears only that call site, not the behavior.\u001b[46C\u001b[39m                                 \u001b[11;1H\u001b[94m3.\u001b[93m pitfall-printable-xor-decode-of-arithmetic-tables\u001b[97m (pitfall, new) — Candidate 4. The self-similar printable run → STL popcount/pshufb table\u001b[39m         \u001b[12;1H\u001b[97mpattern, with closed-form and xref-sweep verification steps; cross-referenced to the related existing pitfall mem-3d4ebcf8.\u001b[39m                           \u001b[13;1H\u001b[94m4.\u001b[93m mem-c893fd1e\u001b[97m (technique, updated via overwrite) — Candidate 1's genuinely novel content (real key = short ASCII \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97mliteral set into a std::string\u001b[39m     \u001b[14;1H\u001b[97mglobal by a pre-main\u001b[93m _initterm\u001b[97m dynamic initializer; 100%-printable-yield confirmation standard) was folded into the existing keystream-reuse memory\u001b[2C\u001b[39m \u001b[15;1H\u001b[97msaved earlier this run.\u001b[94C\u001b[39m                         \u001b[7C \u001b[16;1H\u001b[94m5.\u001b[93m initializer-lea-pair-scan-maps-string-globals\u001b[97m (technique, new) — Candidate 5. The RIP-relative LEA-pair scan of dynamic initializers to produce a\u001b[C\u001b[39m \u001b[17;1H\u001b[97mglobal→plaintext map that makes dynamically-resolved API identities byte-provable; cross-linked to mem-c893fd1e.\u001b[5C\u001b[39m              \u001b[18C \u001b[18;1H \u001b[116C                      \u001b[10C \u001b[19;1H\u001b[36m\u001b[1m## Skipped\u001b[107C\u001b(B\u001b[m                      \u001b[10C \u001b[20;1H \u001b[116C                         \u001b[7C \u001b[21;1H\u001b[97m-\u001b[1m Candidate 1 as a standalone memory\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — its core claim (carved \"keys\" are single-key RC4 ciphertexts) duplicates mem-c893fd1e, the keystream-reuse\u001b[4C\u001b[39m \u001b[22;1H\u001b[97mlesson already saved this run. Rather than create a near-duplicate, I merged its new details into that memory.\u001b[7C\u001b[39m                     \u001b[11C \u001b[23;1H \u001b[116C                 \u001b[15C \u001b[24;1H\u001b[97mThe curation decision record is posted on the forum as\u001b[93m #memory-library-curation\u001b[97m. No sample hashes, paths, decoded C2 values, or session specifics\u001b[39m     \u001b[25;1H\u001b[97mwere saved into cross-run memory (the one deliberate exception: the\u001b[93m builder_v2\u001b[97m assert-path string and IElevator CLSIDs in the family-intel memory,\u001b[39m    \u001b[26;1H\u001b[97mwhich are family-wide build artifacts documented as discriminators, not sample-unique facts).\u001b[24C\u001b[39m            \u001b[20C \u001b[27;1H \u001b[116C                 \u001b[15C \u001b[28;1H\u001b[32m●\u001b[C\u001b[90mmain · ▸ finish() · 64 chars\u001b[87C\u001b[39m                 \u001b[15C \u001b[29;1H \u001b[116C                 \u001b[15C \u001b[30;1H\u001b[97m🤖\u001b[115C\u001b[39m                 \u001b[15C \u001b[31;1H\u001b[97mResuming analysis…\u001b[99C\u001b[39m                 \u001b[15C \u001b[32;1H \u001b[116C                 \u001b[15C \u001b[33;1H\u001b[36m┌\u001b[1m Prompt \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[36m──────────────"]
